# Coverage output from the CI coverage step.
coverage/

# The release pipeline writes a registry token here and removes it again; a
# stray one must never be committable.
.npmrc

# `export-public.mjs` writes this into the directory it builds, and
# `publish-public.mjs` reads it there. It is a handoff between two commands, not
# content: the provenance link that belongs in public history is the
# `Exported-From` trailer on the commit. Ignored so that the `git add -A` in the
# release repository cannot sweep 1000 lines of hashes into every release diff.
#
# Note what an entry here costs: trunk skips an ignored path whether or not git
# tracks it, so anything listed below leaves the trufflehog scan as well. This
# file is written in step 7, after that scan, and holds only hashes and a commit
# id. Never add a path here in order to keep a file out of a build or a
# release — that also removes it from the credential scan.
.export-manifest.json


# Local environment secrets; keep out of every commit.
.env
.realm-plugin/

# A local working checklist, untracked on purpose.
/docs/pushlish-steps.md
